---
title: 'How to Use an AI Job Search Agent: Find, Track and Apply to Jobs From One Chat'
publishedAt: 2026-11-11
type: job-seekers
---
**Quick answer:** An AI job search agent is an assistant you chat with that can take actions in your job search, not just answer questions. On GetHired, the agent searches jobs from many sources using plain-English requests, ranks roles against your resume, tracks your applications and saved jobs, tailors your resume to a specific posting, and sets up mock interviews with feedback. It asks before changing your profile or submitting an application, and AI features use credits shown in your account. Start by uploading your resume, then ask for jobs the way you'd describe them to a friend.

Most job searches are spread across a dozen tabs: job boards, a spreadsheet of applications, a resume file with five versions, notes on interviews. An AI agent pulls those into one conversation. This guide explains what an agent can do, what it can't, and how to get good results from it.

## What is an AI job search agent?

A chatbot answers questions. An agent can also **use tools**: it searches a job database, reads your resume, saves jobs, updates your profile or starts an interview, based on what you ask.

