## What can the GetHired agent do?

### Find jobs from a plain-English description

Instead of fiddling with filters, describe what you want:

- "Remote senior backend roles using Go, paying over $120k."
- "Frontend jobs in Bengaluru or Pune at Series A or B startups, posted this week."
- "Data engineering roles similar to my last job, but at fintech companies."

GetHired lists jobs from company career sites and platforms like Greenhouse, Workday, Lever, Ashby, Y Combinator and Wellfound, so one search covers a lot of ground.

### Find roles that match your resume

Ask "What jobs fit my background best?" and the agent ranks roles against your profile and resume, using meaning rather than exact keywords. It can tell that "built REST APIs in Django" is relevant to a "Python backend engineer" role. Read more on [how semantic matching works](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/why-your-resume-is-getting-ghosted-and-how-semantic-ai-changes-everything).

### Track applications and saved jobs

Ask:

- "What have I applied to this month?"
- "Show my saved jobs at startups."
- "Which applications haven't moved in two weeks?"

That last one pairs well with our [follow-up email templates](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/how-to-follow-up-on-a-job-application-with-email-templates-and-timelines).

### Improve your resume for a specific job

Say "Improve my resume for this job" and the agent compares your resume with the posting, then shows suggested changes (rewritten bullets, additions and removals) in a card. You choose which ones to apply. Nothing changes until you click.

### Practise interviews

Ask the agent to set up an [AI mock interview](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/ai-interview) for a role. You practise by voice and get feedback on your answers afterwards. Your practice interviews stay private.

### Apply to jobs posted on GetHired

For jobs posted directly on GetHired, the agent can read the application form and prepare an Easy Apply. It always shows you a preview and waits for you to approve before submitting. For jobs on other sites, you apply on the employer's site. The [Chrome extension](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/extension) can fill those forms for you to review.

### Remember your preferences

Tell it things like "I won't relocate" or "I'm only interested in companies with fewer than 200 people", and it can save them as memories for future chats.

## How to get good results

### 1. Upload a strong primary resume first

The agent's matches and suggestions are only as good as your resume. Fix formatting issues with the [AI Resume Checker](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/ai-resume-checker) first.

### 2. Be specific about what you want

Include the role, seniority, location or remote preference, salary floor, company stage and must-have technologies. "Jobs for me" is too vague.

### 3. Ask follow-up questions

Treat it like a conversation:

- "Why is the second job a good match?"
- "Only show ones with a published salary."
- "Which of these use TypeScript?"

### 4. Review before you approve

The agent asks before changing your profile, completing onboarding or submitting an application. Read the preview. You're always the one making the decision.

### 5. Keep one search thread per goal

Separate chats for "senior backend roles" and "interview prep for Acme" keep context clean.

## What an AI agent can't do

- **It can't guarantee interviews.** It helps you find and prepare for the right roles; employers still decide.
- **It doesn't apply to jobs on other sites by itself.** You apply on the employer's site.
- **It doesn't know things that aren't in your resume or profile.** If you led a team and it's not written down, tell it.
- **It can make mistakes.** Check job details on the original posting before you apply.

## Is it safe to use an AI job agent?

Look for agents that:

- **Ask before acting.** GetHired asks before changing your profile or submitting an application.
- **Keep your contact details private.** On GetHired, companies browsing the talent pool don't see your email, phone or links until you apply or reply Interested to their message.
- **Treat job post text as untrusted.** GetHired sandboxes job post text so instructions hidden in a posting can't steer the agent.

## Can I use it from Claude, Cursor or another AI assistant?

Yes. The [GetHired MCP server](https://gethired.devhub.co.in/blog/introducing-the-get-hired-mcp-server) connects AI assistants like Claude, Claude Code, Cursor and VS Code to your GetHired account. You sign in with GetHired; there are no API keys. Tools that change things ask you to confirm first.

## Frequently asked questions

### Is the GetHired agent free?

You can start for free. Some AI features, like resume improvements and mock interviews, use credits as shown in your account.

### Does the agent apply to jobs automatically?

No. For jobs posted on GetHired, it prepares the application and shows you a preview, and it submits only after you approve. It never applies on its own.

### Can recruiters see my chats?

No. Your chats with the agent are private. Companies see your public profile only if you make it public, and contact details only when you apply or reply Interested.

### How is an AI job agent different from job alerts?

Job alerts send you listings that match fixed filters. An agent understands requests in plain language, explains matches, refines results in conversation and helps with the next steps, like tailoring your resume.

### What should I ask the agent first?

Upload your resume and ask: "What kinds of roles am I best suited for, and which open jobs fit me best right now?"

